analysis.result:
The authors find that collinear final-state QED radiation from charged leptons induces logarithmic enhancements proportional to $ rac{\alpha}{\pi}\ln\left( rac{E_\ell}{m_\ell}ight)$, modifying the inelasticity $y$ distribution by $-10\%$ at low $y$ up to $+5\%$ at high $y$ for $E_{
u_\mu} = 10^3\,\mathrm{GeV}$. At $E_{
u_\mu} = 10^8\,\mathrm{GeV}$, NLO EW corrections increase the average inelasticity $\langle y angle$ by $\approx 10\%$ (or $\approx 15\%$ when including photon-induced channels). Resonant on-shell $W$-boson production and hidden Glashow processes enhance the high-$y$ region ($y \gtrsim 0.8$) by $> 10\%$ for $E_
u \gtrsim 10^4\,\mathrm{GeV}$. Evaluating QED radiation at the partonic scale $\mu_h^2 = \hat{s}_{12} \sim x s$ avoids an overestimation of $\sim 50\%$ caused by using the hadronic scale $\mu_h^2 = s$.

figures.caption:
Figure 16: Inelasticity distribution $d\sigma/dy$ as a function of the incoming muon-neutrino energy and the muon inelasticity for an isoscalar target. The left panel shows the central NLO QCD prediction, while the right panel shows the NLO QCD $+$ EW prediction including the additional FSR corrections of the lepton FF normalised to the corresponding NLO QCD result. Projections are shown along the corresponding axes: onto $\log_{10}E_{
u_{\mu}}$ (top), i.e. the cross section integrated over $y$, together with the theoretical uncertainties from scale variation, and onto $y$ (right), i.e. $d\sigma/dy$ integrated over $\log_{10}E_{
u_{\mu}}$ in the range $10^{3}\,{m GeV}\leq E_{
u_{\mu}}\leq 10^{7}\,{m GeV}$, for which only the central prediction is shown. Each bin is coloured according to the value of the central prediction in that bin. See main text for further explanations.

